name: mule_structuring
title: "Structuring into one account"
description: "Deposits kept just under a reporting threshold, found by their shape rather than their size. Every transfer stays on the graph with its date and amount, with no amount filter, so each small deposit is still there. Choose BOOKED_AT as the time, then Pattern match ▸ Structuring (amounts from 900 to just under 1,000): it finds exactly one match, twelve accounts paying into one hub account that moves the money on through two relays to an offshore account, and nothing in the ordinary traffic. On Large transfers only, the same pattern says the small deposits were filtered away instead of reporting no match."
sourceId: entity-projection
layout: force
profile: finance
query:
  projection:
    datasetId: mule_transfers_dataset
    sourceCol: PAYER_ACCOUNT
    targetCol: PAYEE_ACCOUNT
    linkKindCol: CHANNEL
    attrCols[2]: BOOKED_AT,AMOUNT
view:
  legend: true
  workingSet: true
  plugins:
    minimap: true
    behaviors[1]: hover-activate
